    {
      "id": "sega-sms-alexkidd-nes-sound",
      "description": "Alex Kidd's PSG replayed on the NES chip FIX. Re-baselined 2026-10-29 (audio only, picture unchanged): APU_FIX no longer resets the triangle's step and timer on a $400B write (nesdev 'APU': there is no way to reset the triangle's phase). The Sega hub sends low PSG voices to the triangle and rewrites $400B whenever a note's period high bits change, so each such note change used to restart the triangle waveform at step 0 (a click and a phase jump); now the waveform runs on through the pitch change as on hardware. Isolated: a build with only the triangle fix gives exactly the new value; the same commit's sweep-mute fix alone changes nothing here.",
      "kind": "session",
      "rom": "{sms}/alexkidd.sms",
      "apu": "NES:FIX",
      "frames": 400,
      "input": "120:A,126:",
      "tags": [
        "sega",
        "sms",
        "bridge",
        "sound"
      ],
      "expect": {
        "exitCode": 0,
